### Fix 4 — AC-7: BLOCKED (nothing landed; `quickbench.py` is byte-identical)
See `BLOCKED.md`. The specified default helper reads `capture_osaurus_settings()` from the real `~/.osaurus/config`, while `tests/test_quickbench.py::test_the_host_pinned_between_pin_and_restore_shows_no_drift` pins a **tmp** config dir; on this host that is 22 drifted keys, the Osaurus cell FAILs, stage B never runs, and `assert len(captured) == 3` fails (observed: `assert 1 == 3`). The order forbids editing that test, and there is no way to give the helper the config dir the caller's `pin` used. `BLOCKED.md` names three decisions, including a pre/post-capture variant that keeps every existing test green.

